//! Parametric sound-effect synthesis.
//!
//! A sound is a spec, not a binary: [`SfxSpec`] plus a seed always renders the
//! same samples, so a catalogue can be regenerated byte for byte at build time
//! instead of shipping audio assets. The eight [`Family`] voices, the named
//! [`PRESETS`] catalogue and the deterministic [`render`] entry were absorbed
//! from the OpenSFX core (Apache-2.0, © OpenSFX Authors) with every constant
//! and every per-family random-consumption order preserved — the golden tests
//! lock the waveforms, not just the shapes.
//!
//! Contracts owned here:
//! - the random stream is `media.dsp::Rng` (xorshift32), the single formal
//!   audio randomness contract of this workspace;
//! - the parameter range contract lives in Rust: `SfxSpec::validate` rejects
//!   out-of-range and non-finite inputs with `Error::invalid_input` instead of
//!   the silent clamping the OpenSFX N-API binding used to apply;
//! - the seed default is one everywhere (`SfxSpec::new`, serde and the
//!   constructor agree on `1`), resolving the historical serde-0 vs new-1
//!   split; `Rng` normalises 0 into the same stream as 1, so no rendered
//!   sound changes because of the unification;
//! - family names are the kebab-case spelling (`Family::as_str` /
//!   `Family::parse`), the authoritative resolution the bindings must reuse.
//!
//! This crate depends only on `media.dsp`, `media.types` and serde. It knows
//! nothing about scenes, track mixing or file formats; composing a rendered
//! voice into a WAV file is the caller's job through `media.codec`.
//!
//! ```rust
//! use media_synthesis::{Family, SfxSpec, render};
//!
//! let spec = SfxSpec::new(Family::Whoosh, 0.9);
//! let samples = render(&spec, 44_100.0).expect("valid spec");
//! assert!(samples.len() > 1000);
//! ```

pub mod spec;
pub mod voices;

pub use spec::{Family, PRESETS, Preset, SfxSpec, preset, preset_names};
pub use voices::render;
